Should we have some configuration on the group that limits the number of devices per user? Just wondering whether it could be a problem to leave it 'unbounded'
If we want to cap, it has to be included at the protocol level because if we leave it to the implementations then they might disagree on the limit and end up forking groups
Perhaps on the same MarmotMultiDevice extension?

```tls
struct {
    uint16 version;              // current: 1                                                                       
    uint8 max_devices_per_user;  // 0 = unlimited, 1-255 = cap                                                       
} MarmotMultiDevice;
```
